From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TR3600 port <local>
Date: Sun, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7996: add WED/RRO configuration for MT7990

Backport MediaTek SDK patch 0048
("mtk: mt76: mt7996: add configuration to suppot wed and rro for mt7990
chipset", fcea34c9147e), which is a prerequisite for SDK patch 0049 and
was missing from the local MT7987 WED hwpath backport.

Problem
-------
mt7996_mmio_wed_init() only special-cased MT7996 when setting up the TX
free done event ring:

	if (is_mt7996(&dev->mt76)) {
		... MT7996_RXQ_TXFREE0 ... MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_MAIN
	} else {
		... MT7996_RXQ_MCU_WA_MAIN ... MT_INT_RX_DONE_WA_MAIN
	}

MT7990 is not MT7996, so it fell into the generic branch and was given
MT7996's txfree ring and interrupt bit. MT7990 has its own TX free done
ring and interrupt (MT7990_RXQ_TXFREE0/1 and
MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_BAND0/1_MT7990, both already defined in this tree and
already used by the non-WED path in mt7996_dma.c).

With the wrong txfree ring the host never sees TX completion, the WED TX
ring is never reclaimed, and TX stalls once it has filled up. Observed
on Cudy TR3600 v1 (MT7987 + MT7990) together with the empty token range
as "Tx attempts 0, PER 100%, SSID not beaconing" once wed_enable is on.

Additionally, mt7996_dma_init() only enabled the MT_RXQ_RRO_BAND1 WED
datapath for MT7992; MT7990 needs it too.

Not validated on hardware yet.

--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -872,7 +872,7 @@ int mt7996_dma_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		if (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76)) {
+		if (!is_mt7996(&dev->mt76)) {
 			dev->mt76.q_rx[MT_RXQ_RRO_BAND1].flags =
 				MT_WED_RRO_Q_DATA(1) | MT_QFLAG_WED_RRO_EN;
 			if (mtk_wed_device_active(wed) &&
--- a/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ b/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -519,11 +519,16 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev, void *pdev_ptr,
 			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base + hif1_ofs +
 						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
 						 MT7996_RXQ_TXFREE2 * MT_RING_SIZE;
-		} else {
+		} else if (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76)) {
 			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_BAND1_EXT) - 1;
 			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base + hif1_ofs +
 						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
 						 MT7996_RXQ_MCU_WA_EXT * MT_RING_SIZE;
+		} else {
+			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_BAND1_MT7990) - 1;
+			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base + hif1_ofs +
+						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
+						 MT7990_RXQ_TXFREE1 * MT_RING_SIZE;
 		}
 
 		wed->wlan.wpdma_rx_glo = wed->wlan.phy_base + hif1_ofs + MT_WFDMA0_GLO_CFG;
@@ -589,13 +594,19 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_dev *dev, void *pdev_ptr,
 		if (is_mt7996(&dev->mt76)) {
 			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base +
 						 MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
 						 MT7996_RXQ_TXFREE0 * MT_RING_SIZE;
 			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_MAIN) - 1;
-		} else {
+		} else if (is_mt7992(&dev->mt76)) {
 			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_DONE_WA_MAIN) - 1;
 			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base + MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
 						  MT7996_RXQ_MCU_WA_MAIN * MT_RING_SIZE;
+		} else {
+			wed->wlan.txfree_tbit = ffs(MT_INT_RX_TXFREE_BAND0_MT7990) - 1;
+			wed->wlan.wpdma_txfree = wed->wlan.phy_base + MT_RXQ_RING_BASE(0) +
+						 MT7990_RXQ_TXFREE0 * MT_RING_SIZE;
+			if (dev->hif2)
+				wed->wlan.id = MT7990_DEVICE_ID;
 		}
 
 		if (dev->hif2 && is_mt7992(&dev->mt76))
 			wed->wlan.id = 0x7992;
